  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.7 - Consume SpawnDev.SpawnJS 2.1.9 so browser consumers get the app-root fix. A consumer of 5.2.5 transitively resolved SpawnJS 2.1.8 and never saw it: SpawnJSInterop normalized a load URL back to the app root by stripping a literal trailing \"_framework/\", so an app that renames that folder (a browser extension may not have a root folder starting with \"_\") got AppBaseUri = the framework folder itself, and every URL built on it - worker entrypoints above all - resolved one level too deep. A 404 worker presents as a crashed renderer, not a clean error. No ILGPU code changed; the fork packages are deliberately unchanged.",
